BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Into the Forest: An Evening for Treehouse
DTSTART:20260828T180000
DTEND:20260828T200000
DTSTAMP:20260828T212739Z
UID:5968f2524fb9301175fd21fc495745@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy a night of community under the canopy at VINS! Walk
  the Canopy Walk at golden hour\, visit with the eagles and owls\, listen 
 to music by Still Hill while enjoying a Wolf Tree cocktail\, and bid on so
 me amazing silent auction items! Sound like your kind of Friday night? We 
 would love to have you come support our community! A major highlight of th
 e evening will be our silent auction! Look forward to silent auction items
  such as: A private cocktail class taught by Max Overstrom-Coleman of Wolf
  Tree A piece of artwork by Ellen Piccolo A guided\, public land Ruffed Gr
 ouse hunt A course in managing child anxiety from a local pediatric anxiet
 y expert Membership to the ECHO Center Gift certificates to The Hop\, Ceda
 r Circle Farm\, Lou's\, Boston Children's Museum\, and Tip Top Pottery.\n
 \nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Institute of Natural Science (VINS)\, 149 Natures Way
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/into-the-f
 orest-an-evening-for-treehouse-04-08-2026-12-33-12
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury: Jon Hayes & the Company
DTSTART:20260828T190000
DTEND:20260828T210000
DTSTAMP:20260828T212739Z
UID:86161f3d06a83e281e425672d7a3f7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Kalamazoo-based songwriter Jon Hayes\, an ascendant star in Mi
 chigan’s indie music scene\, invariably draws comparisons to John Mayer
 \, Bon Iver\, and NEEDTOBREATHE. From basement recordings and house concer
 ts to studio sessions\, live projects\, and multi-city tours\, Jon Hayes &
  the Company captivate fans with soulful vocals\, engaging storytelling\, 
 and an intimate\, startling musicality. Jon Hayes & the Company’s subtle
  melodies and evocative lyrics linger in the mind long after the lights co
 me up. On Friday\, August 28th\, Final Friday festivities begin at 5pm\, w
 hen downtown Railroad Street closes to vehicular traffic to make way for f
 ree\, family-friendly\, all-ages fun. At 7pm\, Jon Hayes & the Company wil
 l take the stage\, wrapping up the last Railroad Street block party of the
  summer with rousing live music and dancing. Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury will
  return to Dog Mountain on Sunday\, August 30th\, for the final show of th
 e 2026 series\, featuring unexpectedly infectious harp-infused hip-hop fro
 m Küf Knotz and Christine Elise\, at 5pm. The Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury Li
 ve Music Series\, presented by Catamount Arts with support from the Levitt
  Family Foundation\, began in 2017 as a free\, family-friendly (and dog-fr
 iendly) weekly concert series at Dog Mountain\, St. Johnsbury’s beloved 
 150-acre dog park known for its hiking trails\, art gallery\, dog chapel\,
  and community events. Catamount Arts has since partnered with Discover St
 . Johnsbury to include additional Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury concerts at Fin
 al Fridays events in June\, July\, and August. All Levitt AMP St. Johnsbur
 y concerts are free\, accessible\, and appropriate for all ages. Dogs are 
 welcome! Food and beverages\, including beer and cocktails\, will be avail
 able for purchase. Picnics are welcome at Dog Mountain\, but please note t
 hat no outside alcohol is permitted at either Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury ven
 ue. For more information\, including the full concert line-up\, visit www.
 catamountarts.org. Downtown St. Johnsbury\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/levitt-amp
 -st-johnsbury-jon-hayes-the-company-24-08-2026-11-18-50
END:VEVENT
